  "notes": [
    "IFRS throughout. revenue = Sales (the top line of Roche's multi-year overview); it excludes royalties/other revenue (CHF 1,840m in 2025), which is why Yahoo's total revenue is ~3% higher in 2025. Net income and EPS match Yahoo for 2025.",
    "Each year taken from the latest Finance Report that presents it (comparative column of the following report where available); EPS, dividend and employees from the Multi-year overview tables (as reported).",
    "totalDebt = long-term + short-term debt (the \"Total debt\" line of the debt note). capex = purchase of property, plant and equipment only (purchase of intangible assets is reported separately, e.g. CHF 2,031m in 2025).",
    "sharesOutstanding = number of shares plus non-voting equity securities (Genussscheine) issued; 160m bearer shares until 2021, 106.691m after the cancellation of shares bought back from Novartis (Dec 2021), plus 702,562,700 NES.",
    "employees: 2007-2020 number of employees at year end (multi-year overview); 2021-2024 full-time equivalents from Annual Reports 2021-2025; 2025 is a headcount (112,774) on a broader ESRS scope, not comparable with the 2024 FTE figure (103,249).",
    "dividendPerShare for 2025 is the amount proposed by the Board.",
    "Finance Reports 2008-2014 are no longer on roche.com; the citations are Wayback Machine copies of the original roche.com PDFs.",
    "Yahoo comparison: 2025 NI 12,869 vs 12,880 reported; earlier Yahoo years are converted at historical rates so the CHF ratios differ; revenue/NI ratios are consistent with total revenue incl. other revenue."
  ]
